    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189563": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Information Systems (2 positions)",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Assistant/Associate Professor in Information Systems (2 positions) Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management - IS group Location Hong Kong Open Date Jul 15, 2026 Description The Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management (ISOM) at the HKUST Business School invites applications for two tenure-track assistant professor/associate professor positions in the Information Systems area beginning in July 2027. Established in 1991, the HKUST Business School is ranked among the Top Business Schools in the world in terms of research, educational programs, and student and graduate quality. The IS group (with 18 tenure-track faculty) is ranked #20 for publications in ISR and MISQ (2021-2025), while HKUST Business School is ranked #27 in the UT Dallas Journals Ranking (2021-2025). Our MBA programs have been consistently ranked among the top in the world. Ranked 4th in Global Executive MBA program for 2025 (Joint program with Kellogg of Northwestern University; Financial Times) Ranked 24th in Global MBA programs for 2026 (Financial Times) Asia's No 1 by Bloomberg Businessweek (2024-2025) For further information on HKUST Business School, please visit https://bm.hkust.edu.hk/ Qualifications Candidates must have received a doctorate in Information Systems or a related area by May 2027. The candidates must also have a strong commitment to high-quality research and excellent teaching. The successful candidate should have the ability to teach at both the MBA and undergraduate levels. Candidates preferably will be able to do both research and teach courses in the following areas: Cybersecurity  [Note: We are offering a new MSc in Information and Cybersecurity Management] AI, ML, Fintech  [Note: We are in the process of creating a joint HKUST-Tsinghua Research Center for the AI Economy] Health IT  [Note: HKUST is setting up a medical school] Application Instructions Applicants should apply online via Interfolio with CV and supporting documents (e.g. teaching and research statement, 3 reference letters, etc.). Applications will be considered till positions are filled. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interview. Interviews will be conducted on a rolling basis. For enquiry, please contact infosys@ust.hk Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. Howev