    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189501": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Tenure-Track Faculty Positions Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Department of Ocean Science Location Hong Kong Open Date Jul 14, 2026 Description The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST), a world-class research institution, invites applications for tenure-track positions at all ranks within the Department of Ocean Science. We welcome outstanding candidates in all disciplines of ocean science and technology, and particularly encourage applications at the Associate Professor to Full Professor levels with research expertise in: ocean biogeochemical modeling; ocean-atmosphere interactions; cryosphere dynamics; climate variability and change; ocean remote sensing and technology; AI and data-driven oceanography; biological oceanography with a focus on higher trophic organisms; blue economy inclusive of fishery sciences. About Department of Ocean Science The Department of Ocean Science (OCES), established in 2018, is the only ocean-focused department among local universities in Hong Kong, and is committed to multidisciplinary research and education in ocean science and technology. Located in the Clear Water Bay, HKUST offers a distinctive advantage as the only university in Hong Kong with an on-campus waterfront Ocean Research Facility (OCRF)—an exceptional platform enabling innovative ocean and environmental research. We pursue studies spanning from fundamental sciences to cutting-edge technologies, while actively connecting scientific knowledge with real-world impacts through collaborations with governmental and industrial partners. We play a leading role in ocean science at the local, regional, and international levels. Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD degree in ocean science or a closely related discipline. For Assistant Professor positions, at least 2 years of post-doctoral experience is preferred.  Successful candidates should demonstrate strong research records, the potential to establish strong research programs, and a commitment to excellence in teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. The medium of instruction is English at HKUST. Appointment Terms Initial appointment is typically on a three-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. Eligible candidates at the rank of Associate Professor or above may be granted substantiated (tenured) appointments at HKUST, subject to a positive outcome through the University’s formal academic review and approval processes. A gratuity is payable upon successful completion of the contract. HKUST offers an internationally competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits; housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. The University is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty and has a range of family-friendly policies in place. Application Instructions Application materials including a cover letter, detailed curriculum vitae, research accomplishment and proposal (maximum 3 pages), three representative publications (for Assistant Professor level) / five representative publications (for Associate Professor level and above) , teaching statement (maximum 1 page), and at least 3 letters from referees, should be submitted as part of the application through Interfolio.  The recruitment process will continue until all positions are filled. Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website and by clicking the “Apply Now”: https://apply.interfolio.com/189501 Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application. HKUST is a world-class research institution with over 700 faculty members whose research ranges from science and engineering to business and social sciences.  Located in the Clear Water Bay area, HKUST’s campus has a magnificent ocean view and immediate access to a wide range of marine habitats for research and teaching. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for