    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187270": {
      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Drug Discovery and Translational Therapeutics Faculty Positions Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location Hong Kong Open Date Jun 12, 2026 Description The Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seeks outstanding candidates for faculty positions in Drug Discovery and Translational Therapeutics , a key focus area supported by established strengths in biotechnology and related disciplines. The research environment enables effective translation of fundamental discoveries into therapeutic applications. Research areas include: Target identification and validation Drug discovery, pharmacology, and chemical biology Mechanisms of action and therapeutic pathways Translational pipelines linking discovery to preclinical and clinical development The Division is recruiting multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty members to advance its mission of understanding the mechanisms underlying human health and disease through both basic and translational research. Outstanding candidates at both junior and senior levels will be considered. Successful applicants are expected to establish independent, internationally competitive research programs and contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Division of Life Science The Division of Life Science has established strengths across seven thematic areas: (i) Neuroscience and Nervous System Disorders, (ii) Cancer Biology, (iii) Cell Biology and Signaling, (iv) Stem Cell and Developmental Biology, (v) Macromolecular Structure and Function, (vi) Biotechnology and Medicinal Biochemistry, and (vii) Genomics and Epigenomics. These interconnected themes foster extensive cross-disciplinary collaboration across the life sciences. Faculty members are internationally recognized, and the Division is supported by world-class research infrastructure at HKUST, including the Biosciences Central Research Facility , the Biological Cryo-EM Center , the Laboratory Animal Facility , and a state-of-the-art AI Supercomputing Facility . The Division also offers vibrant postgraduate programs and strong global and industry partnerships. HKUST is a globally recognized research university at the forefront of science, engineering, and business. The University is advancing the development of a new, technology-driven Medical School, offering unique opportunities for interdisciplinary and translational research. Beyond academia, HKUST fosters a dynamic innovation ecosystem, including a strong portfolio of start-ups and high-impact ventures. The University is committed to the values of Excellence, Integrity, and Academic Freedom. Qualifications Applicants should possess: A Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree Completion of postdoctoral training Demonstrated potential to lead an independent, externally funded research program Application Instructions Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae A three-page research statement and a one-page teaching statement Names and contact details of three referees Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website: https://apply.interfolio.com/187270 (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ 